{
    "background_story": "Zaniyah was a brilliant and resourceful engineer who specialized in designing innovative solutions for people with disabilities. Growing up, she had witnessed her mother struggle with occlusive vascular disease, which limited her mobility and independence. Determined to make a difference, Zaniyah dedicated herself to creating assistive technologies that could improve the lives of others with similar conditions. Her breakthrough invention, a smart prosthetic limb, was designed to detect and respond to occlusive events, preventing blood clots and promoting healthy circulation. Zaniyah's work not only improved the quality of life for countless individuals but also earned her international recognition and accolades. Her selfless dedication to helping others overcome the challenges of occlusive diseases inspired a new generation of engineers and researchers.",
